From 6a311563e152d352cf4978e025f7a17852fd0802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mxstrk <Maximilian.stark@tuhh.de>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:28:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] la9310shiva: port la9310_modinfo from NXP mainline

RFNM's shiva fork predates NXP's modinfo interface, so /dev/shiva0 and
IOCTL_LA93XX_MODINFO_GET do not exist and the NXP host tools (iq_app,
iq_mon, iq_trace, la9310_modem_info, vspa_mbox) have no way to learn the
HIF/CCSR/iqflood addresses. Port the mainline la9310_modinfo.c onto this
fork so those tools run on the RFNM stack unchanged.

Fork-specific differences are documented in the file header: the misc
device is registered as shiva%d (la9310_dev->name is nlm%d here), the
scratch buffer comes from a module parameter instead of the absent
scratch_buf_host_phys_addr, iqflood is the fixed RFNM carveout, and the
rfcal region does not exist.

Registration failure is non-fatal - only the NXP tools depend on the
device, so a probe that cannot create it still brings the radio up.

Built against rfnm/imx8mp-kernel@rfnm_6.6.36 with the board's own config.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
